A slot machine shows a three-digit number. Its hundreds digit is 8, its tens digit is 5, and its units digit is \(X\).
The machine pays:
5 shekels if the number is divisible by 2 but not by 3;
10 shekels if it is divisible by 3 but not by 2;
15 shekels if it is divisible by both 2 and 3.
Maya played once and won 15 shekels. How many different values can \(X\) have?
